+# Rethlas with OpenCode
+
+[简体中文](README.opencode.zh-CN.md)
+
+This is an additive OpenCode runtime for Rethlas. The original Codex
+configuration, agents, scripts, and documentation remain unchanged.
+
+## Runtime layout
+
+The two entry points are:
+
+- generation: `agents/generation/tests/run_example_opencode.sh`
+- verification API: `agents/verification/api/server_opencode.py`
+
+OpenCode-specific configuration lives in:
+
+- `agents/generation/opencode.json`
+- `agents/verification/opencode.json`
+
+Shared `AGENTS.md`, generic skills, MCP Python servers, problem data, schemas,
+and the Zola result site are reused.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+Install OpenCode, then connect your own coding plan or API provider. The patch
+does not hardcode a provider or model. When no per-run model is supplied,
+OpenCode uses the model selected by your own user-level configuration.
+
+Check the installation, authentication state, and available models:
+
+```bash
+opencode --version
+opencode auth list
+opencode models
+```
+
+Use `/connect` in the OpenCode TUI to sign in to a supported plan or configure
+an API provider. Keep API keys in OpenCode's user-level credential store; do
+not put them in this repository.
+
+## 1. Start the OpenCode verification service
+
+Create the verification environment:
+
+```bash
+cd agents/verification
+python3 -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
+
+Start the OpenCode-backed API on the same local-only port used by the Codex
+workflow:
+
+```bash
+uvicorn api.server_opencode:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8091
+```
+
+Do not run the Codex and OpenCode verification APIs simultaneously because
+both use port 8091.
+
+## 2. Run the included example
+
+In another terminal:
+
+```bash
+cd agents/generation
+python3 -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate
+pip install -r mcp/requirements.txt
+./tests/run_example_opencode.sh
+```
+
+The OpenCode runner:
+
+- runs `opencode run` in `agents/generation`
+- parses the OpenCode JSON event stream for the session id
+- resumes the same session with `--session`
+- alternates retrieval-disabled and retrieval-enabled agents
+- enables OpenCode web search through `OPENCODE_ENABLE_EXA=1`
+- stops when the OpenCode-isolated verified blueprint exists
+
+For `data/example.md`, OpenCode uses:
+
+```text
+problem_id=opencode/example
+memory/opencode/example/
+results/opencode/example/
+logs/opencode/example/
+```
+
+The Codex workflow continues to use `problem_id=example`, so the two sets of
+generation artifacts do not collide.
+
+## 3. Run another problem
+
+```bash
+PROBLEM_FILE=data/modrep/modrep.md ./tests/run_example_opencode.sh
+```
+
+The original reference-directory convention is preserved:
+
+```text
+data/modrep/modrep.md
+data/modrep/modrep.refs/
+```
+
+## Provider and model configuration
+
+With no environment override, generation and verification each use OpenCode's
+configured default model. To pin a model for either process without editing
+project files, use its OpenCode `provider/model` id:
+
+```bash
+OPENCODE_GENERATION_MODEL="provider/model" \
+  ./tests/run_example_opencode.sh
+```
+
+```bash
+OPENCODE_VERIFICATION_MODEL="provider/model" \
+  uvicorn api.server_opencode:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8091
+```
+
+Generation and verification are separate OpenCode processes. Set both
+variables when you want both sides pinned to the same model.
+
+Only set a variant when the selected model exposes that variant:
+
+```bash
+OPENCODE_GENERATION_VARIANT=high ./tests/run_example_opencode.sh
+```
+
+```bash
+OPENCODE_VERIFICATION_VARIANT=high \
+  uvicorn api.server_opencode:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8091
+```
+
+Leave `OPENCODE_GENERATION_MODEL`, `OPENCODE_VERIFICATION_MODEL`, and their
+variant variables unset to use the user's OpenCode configuration.
+
+## OpenCode compatibility layer
+
+OpenCode automatically discovers the existing generic skills under
+`.agents/skills/`. It also loads:
+
+- `AGENTS.opencode.md` through the `instructions` field
+- `.opencode/skills/recursive-proving-opencode/SKILL.md`
+
+The compatibility instructions map the MCP-prefixed OpenCode tool names and
+replace the Codex-specific recursive-proving skill. All other shared skills
+remain unchanged. The replacement skill carries an explicit recursion counter
+in task prompts. A three-agent permission chain prevents child-task creation
+beyond depth 3.
+
+## Return to Codex
+
+The original commands are unchanged:
+
+```bash
+cd agents/verification
+uvicorn api.server:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8091
+```
+
+```bash
+cd agents/generation
+./tests/run_example.sh
+```
