+---
+name: recursive-proving-opencode
+description: Launch one OpenCode subagent per decomposition plan after direct screening has identified the key stuck points for each plan. Use when all current plans have been screened by direct proving, none fully solves the problem, and parallel recursive work is needed.
+compatibility: opencode
+---
+
+# Recursive Proving with OpenCode
+
+Use this skill when direct proving has failed on every current decomposition
+plan. This is the OpenCode counterpart of the Codex-specific
+`recursive-proving` skill.
+
+## Input contract
+
+Read:
+
+- the current set of decomposition plans
+- the direct-proving reports and key stuck points for each plan
+- the known stuck points from other plans
+- relevant `failed_paths`, `branch_states`, and search results
+
+## Procedure
+
+1. Confirm that every current decomposition plan has already been attempted
+   with `$direct-proving` and that none has fully solved the problem.
+2. Use OpenCode's `task` tool to invoke one `subgoal-prover` subagent per
+   decomposition plan. Set `recursion_depth=1` and
+   `maximum_recursion_depth=3` in every initial task prompt.
+3. Give each subagent:
+   - the complete target theorem
+   - the exact OpenCode `problem_id`
+   - its assigned decomposition plan
+   - the key stuck points for its own plan
+   - the key stuck points found in the other plans
+   - the current `recursion_depth` and `maximum_recursion_depth=3`
+   - the instruction to follow `AGENTS.md` and `AGENTS.opencode.md`
+4. Tell each subagent to continue from the assigned plan rather than restart
+   the search from zero. It may refine or locally revise the plan when evidence
+   justifies that change, but it must preserve continuity with the assigned
+   approach.
+5. A subagent may recurse through the `task` tool only when recursion is
+   genuinely useful:
+   - `subgoal-prover` at depth 1 may invoke `subgoal-prover-depth-2`.
+   - `subgoal-prover-depth-2` may invoke `subgoal-prover-depth-3`.
+   - `subgoal-prover-depth-3` cannot create another child task.
+   The child prompt must increment `recursion_depth` by one. At depth 3,
+   continue locally.
+6. Require every subagent to write progress, failures, and successful proof
+   developments to shared memory using the same OpenCode-prefixed `problem_id`.
+7. Delegate independent plans independently. Gather every returned report
+   before selecting the next parent action.
+8. If any plan succeeds, assemble the proof draft from that plan.
+9. If all plans fail, hand the collected reports to
+   `$identify-key-failures`.
+
+## Output contract
+
+Append an `events` record for the recursive round:
+
+```json
+{
+  "event_type": "recursive_proving_round",
+  "plan_ids": ["..."],
+  "subagent_ids": ["..."],
+  "shared_stuck_points": {
+    "plan_id": ["..."]
+  },
+  "status": "running|completed",
+  "successful_plan_ids": ["..."],
+  "failed_plan_ids": ["..."]
+}
+```
+
+Update `branch_states` with the recursive round status and per-plan outcomes.
+
+## Tools
+
+- OpenCode `task` tool using the `subgoal-prover` subagent
+- `reasoning_agent_memory_search`
+- `reasoning_agent_memory_append`
+- `reasoning_agent_branch_update`
+- `reasoning_agent_search_arxiv_theorems` when search is allowed
+
+## Failure logging
+
+If every plan fails in the recursive round, append a summary record to
+`failed_paths` and immediately invoke `$identify-key-failures`.
