@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# OpenCode Compatibility Instructions
+
+This file supplements `AGENTS.md` only for OpenCode runs. Follow all base
+instructions in `AGENTS.md`; use the mappings and overrides below when the base
+instructions use Codex-specific names.
+
+## Isolated problem ids
+
+The OpenCode runner supplies an explicit `problem_id` beginning with
+`opencode/`. Use that exact id for every memory and result operation. Do not
+strip the prefix. Reference directories remain under `data/` and do not gain
+the prefix.
+
+For example:
+
+- input: `data/example.md`
+- OpenCode problem id: `opencode/example`
+- memory: `memory/opencode/example/`
+- results: `results/opencode/example/`
+
+## MCP tool names
+
+OpenCode prefixes tools from the `reasoning_agent` MCP server. Interpret the
+unprefixed tool names in `AGENTS.md` and shared skills as follows:
+
+- `search_arxiv_theorems` -> `reasoning_agent_search_arxiv_theorems`
+- `verify_proof_service` -> `reasoning_agent_verify_proof_service`
+- `memory_init` -> `reasoning_agent_memory_init`
+- `memory_append` -> `reasoning_agent_memory_append`
+- `memory_search` -> `reasoning_agent_memory_search`
+- `branch_update` -> `reasoning_agent_branch_update`
+
+Always call the prefixed OpenCode tool name when it is available.
+
+## Recursive proving
+
+When `AGENTS.md` calls for `$recursive-proving`, load and follow
+`$recursive-proving-opencode` instead. Do not load the Codex-specific
+`$recursive-proving` skill.
+
+Use OpenCode's `task` tool with the `subgoal-prover` subagent for recursive
+proof work. Independent decomposition plans should be delegated independently,
+and all returned reports must be gathered before the parent chooses its next
+step. Pass an explicit recursion depth in each task prompt and stop spawning
+children at depth 3, as specified by `$recursive-proving-opencode`. The
+`subgoal-prover` → `subgoal-prover-depth-2` →
+`subgoal-prover-depth-3` permission chain enforces this limit.
+
+## Search terminology
+
+References to "Codex built-in web search" mean OpenCode's `websearch` tool.
+Use `webfetch` to retrieve a known page or paper URL. During turns run with the
+`rethlas-no-search` agent, search tools are intentionally unavailable; continue
+with local memory and independent reasoning.
